PsychoPy movement extraction and merging workflow -> Step 2

Purpose

Create an auditable participant-level movement master from standardized PsychoPy
files without modifying source data.

Script

`scripts/psychopy/s_file_merging.R`

Input

`data/s_files/psychopy/ID_Block_Condition.csv`

- ID format: two letters, two digits, two letters, two digits.
- Block: A or B; A was measured first and B second.
- Condition: HB or LB.
- Each ID should have exactly two files: one HB, one LB, one A, and one B.
- The standardized filename is authoritative for ID, Block, and Condition.

Outputs

All outputs are written to `data/inter/psychopy`:

- `file_validation.csv`: filename, participant-pair, and file-level validation.
- `psychopy_movement_audit.csv`: one row per file and trial, including raw
  lists, raw/adjusted counts, artifact decisions, unmatched timestamps, and
  warnings/errors.
- `psychopy_measurement_summary.csv`: one row per measurement file; normally
  two rows per participant.
- `psychopy_master.csv`: one row per participant with HB/LB trial counts,
  condition totals, and `trial_order`.

The master is created only when no critical validation error remains. It stays
in the intermediate folder until reviewed; approved data can later be moved to
`data/processed/psychopy/master`.

Procedure

1. Discover all CSV files directly inside `data/s_files/psychopy`.
2. Parse ID, Block, and Condition from each standardized filename.
3. Validate filenames and check for duplicate ID-Block-Condition files.
4. Confirm each ID has exactly one A, one B, one HB, and one LB file.
5. For trials 01-04, locate the populated columns matching:
   `Klicks_Block_[A/B]_[trial].clicked_name` and `.time`.
6. Accept either A or B inside the raw column name. Compare it with the
   authoritative filename Block and report disagreements as warnings.
7. Parse list contents without evaluating code. Standardize movement names to
   arm, head, leg, and other. Unknown names or unreadable/missing trial data
   become NA and block creation of the final master.
8. Apply the early-event rule below.
9. Count adjusted arm, head, leg, other, and total movements for every trial.
10. Create the measurement summary, then reshape HB and LB into one participant
    row.
11. Derive `trial_order`: `HB_LB` means HB was Block A; `LB_HB` means LB was
    Block A.
12. Add arm, head, leg, other, and all-movement totals across trials 01-04 for
    HB and LB separately.

Early-event rule

The threshold is strictly below 0.01 seconds.

- If the first timestamp is not below 0.01 seconds, remove nothing.
- If the first timestamp is below 0.01 seconds, remove that timestamp.
- Also remove the first clicked name only when the raw timestamp count equals
  the raw clicked-name count. In that case, the first entries are treated as a
  paired system artifact.
- When timestamps outnumber clicked names, retain every clicked name because
  the CSV cannot identify which timestamps were unnamed.
- Record remaining unmatched timestamps; do not assign them to movement names.
- Final summary/master files contain adjusted counts only. Raw and adjusted
  values remain available in the movement audit.
- A valid empty clicked-name list means zero movements. Missing, invalid, or
  unreadable data means NA, never zero.

Validation and review

`REVIEW_REQUIRED`

- Critical problem: invalid filename, duplicate measurement, incomplete
  participant design, or failed trial extraction.
- Validation and audit files are still written.
- `psychopy_master.csv` is not created until the problem is resolved.

`VALID_WITH_WARNING`

- Counts remain usable, but a documented issue exists, such as unmatched
  timestamps or an internal A/B header that differs from the filename.
- The file remains in summaries and the master.

`VALID`

- No critical issue or warning was found.

Expected documented warnings

The following warnings were identified while inspecting the retained raw data.
Standardized filenames are shown.

- `AN15AV09_A_LB.csv`, trial 02: one timestamp remains unmatched after removing
  the early timestamp. Retain all clicked names; do not assign the timestamp.
- `CH10AL22_B_HB.csv`, trial 01: one timestamp remains unmatched after removing
  the early timestamp. Retain all clicked names; do not assign the timestamp.
- `JE06AD10_A_LB.csv`, trial 03: one timestamp remains unmatched after removing
  the early timestamp. Retain all clicked names; do not assign the timestamp.
- `MA25UT20_B_LB.csv`, trial 03: one timestamp remains unmatched after removing
  the early timestamp. Retain all clicked names; do not assign the timestamp.
- `SA09OR12_A_LB.csv`, trial 03: three timestamps remain unmatched after
  removing the early timestamp. Retain all clicked names; do not assign the
  timestamps.
- `LE11ON12_B_LB.csv`, trials 01-04: internal columns contain Block A because of
  the previously documented system error. Use Block B from the standardized
  filename; retain and count the populated trial columns.

These warnings document uncertainty but do not justify deleting named movement
events. Confirm the exact warnings against the newly generated audit after each
run because the input folder may change.

Manual warning-resolution log

Copy one block per new or changed warning:


- File: ______________________________________________
  Trial: __________
  Audit warning: _____________________________________
  Evidence reviewed: _________________________________
  Decision: __________________________________________
  Data change made: __________________________________
  Reviewer/date: _____________________________________

  -> no manual warning resolutions necessary

Final approval

- [ ] `file_validation.csv` contains no `REVIEW_REQUIRED` rows.
- [ ] Every warning in `psychopy_movement_audit.csv` has been reviewed or
      accepted under the documented rule.
- [ ] Each ID has one HB and one LB measurement.
- [ ] Each ID has a valid `HB_LB` or `LB_HB` trial order.
- [ ] Trial totals equal arm + head + leg + other.
- [ ] HB/LB condition totals equal the sums of trials 01-04.
- [ ] Participant count and IDs match the expected study sample.
- [ ] Only after these checks, move the approved master to
      `data/processed/psychopy/master`.
